  "summary": "A traditional Japanese theatrical makeup style using bold lines and symbolic colors to represent character traits and emotions in Kabuki theater.",
  "description": "Features bold lines in red, blue, brown, and black applied to the face and neck; colors represent character types with red indicating heroism and blue indicating villainy. Developed during the Edo period to visually distinguish characters and their roles from a distance in large theaters.",
